#ARTIST be-music
#GENRE TEST
#BPM 120
#PLAYLEVEL 3
#TOTAL 300
#DIFFICULTY 2

*---------------------- EXTENDED HEADER FIELD
* Keyboardmania-style 24 KEY SP. The 24 lanes live on the classic 1P
* columns `11..19` plus the extended columns `1A..1O` (lane 10 = `1A`
* … lane 24 = `1O`). One extended channel is enough for
* `resolveChartPlayVariant` to classify the chart as `'24'`, so the
* `.bme` extension does NOT pull it back to 7 KEY SP and channels
* `16` / `17` stay ordinary lanes instead of scratch / FREE ZONE.
*
* This chart exists to validate:
*   - extended lane channels are extracted as scorable playable notes
*   - `24 KEY SP` lane-mode detection and its 24 key bindings
*   - long notes (`#LNOBJ`) and landmines on extended channels
*   - the fallback playfield laying out 24 lanes without a scratch column

#PLAYER 1
#LNTYPE 1
#LNMODE 1
#LNOBJ ZZ

*---------------------- RESOURCES FIELD

#WAV01 sample.wav
#WAVZZ sample.wav

